{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503278-building-a-pseudo-theurge-using-kinfolk-w20-rules","id":1503278,"title":"Building a pseudo-Theurge using Kinfolk W20 rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-16T17:06:39-08:00","id":1503278,"title":"Building a pseudo-Theurge using Kinfolk W20 rules","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> I've playing with the idea of trying (emphasis on trying) to build a kinfolk character that can act as a second-class Theurge for the pack. I wanted to see how far you can stretch the available options until you reach the natural limitation that Kinfolks have<br /> <br /> I'm planning on building it with Social as primary attributes (important for Hedge Magic and Rites) an Knowledges as primary abilities (same reason as the previous one). More specifically, this character will have Rituals as high as possible, allowing him to learn Garou rites.<br /> <br /> As for backgrounds, a emphasis on Rites would be the preference. As high as allowed by the ST. <br /> <br /> Finally, using the freebies, this character would max Gnosis (7pts) and take two points on Spiritual Chasing (with a connection to a wolf-spirit or some spirit that fall in the umbrella of his related tribe totem) (14pts). If there's space for some flaws, the additional frebies would be used to buy Lingering Kin-Fetch (2pts).<br /> <br /> Some questions for you:<br /> - Do you see another avenue to get a character like that closer to the sthereotipical Theurge skills/abilities?<br /> - Regarding Rites, the writing of the background for kinfolks is a little strange for me. Can Kinfolks learn / use Garou Rites up to level 2? This would be great because there are powerful rites within that range.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26085-raphaelrrcoelho","name":"raphaelrrcoelho","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T06:28:09-08:00","id":1503522,"title":"","content":"I tried to make a Kinfolk character with Gnosis / Gifts / Numina once (albeit under Revised rules) and sadly, it did not work out great within a group of Garou characters. Because even though during character creation I thought I could make the character useful by giving them enough points in Gifts and Gnosis, in practice they turned out to be a liability for the pack.<br /> <br /> My mistake here was trying to emulate being a Garou, instead of complementing the pack's abilities - Kinfolk are human, and oh so fragile. As advice I would say focus less on Gifts and Gnosis, and try the shaman route instead, focusing on Numina and Rites. Rites aren't capped, and with ST agreement you can use the W20 rules for learning Garou Rites. With Numina you may also gain access to Rituals, which is another thing you could bring to the table.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's an option for you, but Sorcerer plays pretty well with Werewolf. I run a mixed group and the Sorcery Paths have a bit more oomph to them and are versatile enough to emulate a Theurge's style.<br /> <br /> One thing I could see working well for Kinfolk is Channeling (ie, invite a spirit to use your body to do something). This basically gives the ST control of the power level of the channeled abilities, and it's thematically fitting for emulating Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T15:58:30-08:00","id":1503704,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions.<br /> <br /> I agree that a build focused on rites and Numina seems rather more useful (and interesting).<br /> <br /> By the W20 rule, with a starting knowledge of Rituals 3, you could get Rite of Summoning and Cleasing, for instance. This would already bring a lot of usefulness. Also, the minor rites for kinfolks are powerful in their own way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought about acquiring two levels of Spirit Chasing to further the relationship of the kinfolk with spirits. For example, you could align with the pack's totem to justify your closeness with them.<br /> <br /> The merit of Lingerinf Kin-Fetch would also go in this direction. The more this kinfolk is connected to the umbra and has relationships with spirits, the more I feel it would (tematically) help as the shaman of the pack.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26085-raphaelrrcoelho","name":"raphaelrrcoelho","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T14:12:10-08:00","id":1503914,"title":"","content":"If you have access to one of the sourcebooks that detail the Paths of Sorcery, the best thing to do is give that character the path of Ephemera. That allows them to do most of the things you would want a Theurge to do with nature spirits. And if you wanted to expand the character's ability to deal with other kinds of spirits, or some of the other abilities of a Theurge (like healing), then you can find other paths for them too. Trying to make it using the normal Kinfolk rules just isn't going to work out in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The original 1997 World of Darkness: Sorcerer book is something I have gotten a lot of use out of the years for multiple game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T12:00:04-08:00","id":1504130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503278-building-a-pseudo-theurge-using-kinfolk-w20-rules?p=1503914#post1503914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemera</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call on that, probably one of the most useful hedge magic paths. Most recent version is in Sorcerer 20, albeit without the <i>really</i> useful example rituals from earlier iterations.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503278-building-a-pseudo-theurge-using-kinfolk-w20-rules?p=1503914#post1503914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to make it using the normal Kinfolk rules just isn't going to work out in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have to agree. If one of my players wanted to try a kinfolk character, I would probably use my house rules for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults?p=1493810#post1493810\">witchcraft </a>(which is basically just a Garou/Fera template sans shapeshifting and Rage).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T05:18:10-08:00","id":1527653,"title":"","content":"I'm very late to the convo, but perhaps making a Kinfolk that becomes a Kami may be the solution here. If Invulnerability is one of your Kami's Powers, it would enable the Kinfolk to be more involved on the ground with their Garou kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}